<HEAD2>Projects</HEAD2>
Each of the following project is a group project to be done by around 5 students each. Each
 project will be done by multiple
 groups. Each group does one project. Groups shown with <RED><TICK/></RED> are already confirmed. The other groups are created arbitrarily
 by me (and open to negotiation until  20th Sep, 2026).
<OL>
<LI>Box-Muller transform and other related simulation techniques
<BR/><B>Topics to be covered:</B>  Box-Muller transform with proof, inverse CDF method, rejection sampling.
 You must actually write some code to implement these techniques and show the code and run it to
 produce output during the presentation.<BR/>
<B>Resource:</B>  Just Google search would give you enough material.
<UL>
</UL>
</LI>
<LI>Face recognition using eigenanalysis (computational aspect, moderate).
<BR/><B>Topics to be covered:</B>  Explain how eigenvalues and eigenvectors help to find the
 directions and amounts of scatter. Explain image data. 
 You must actually write some code to implement these techniques and show the code and run it to
 produce output during your presentation.<BR/>
<B>Resource:</B>  <LINK  to="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLx--gUxue3Z-QL_BG8VeN4Ji1JcH7jUMK">See this youtube playlist</LINK>. Also you
 can download a relevant data set from <LINK to="grayfaces.tar.gz">here</LINK>.
